# Shell scripts must keep LF endings regardless of platform.
#
# This checkout has core.autocrlf=true. Without these rules a fresh clone gets
# CRLF endings, and a `#!/bin/sh` script with CRLF fails on Linux/macOS with a
# misleading "bad interpreter" error -- for a git hook that means it silently
# does not run.
.githooks/** text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
